{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4637196","formula":"C₁₁H₉N₃O","hill":"C11H9N3O","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":9.0,"N":3.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"4-Pyridylnicotinamide"},"descriptions":{"en":"4-Pyridylnicotinamide (4-PNA), also known as N-(pyridin-4-yl)nicotinamide, is a kinked dipodal dipyridine which was originally developed for use in chemotherapy. As in its isomer 3-pyridylnicotinamide, the nitrogen atoms on its pyridine rings can donate their electron lone pairs to metal cations, allowing it to bridge metal centers and act as a bidentate ligand in coordination polymers. It is synthesized through the reaction of nicotinoyl chloride and 4-aminopyridine."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":3049109,"mass":199.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC(=CN=C1)C(=O)NC2=CC=NC=C2","inchikey":"HVLLFBPOFNSPRN-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-pyridin-4-ylpyridine-3-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3049109","atoms":24,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.211,"y":-1.827,"z":-0.302,"el":"O"},{"x":0.46,"y":0.4,"z":0.048,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.542,"y":1.503,"z":-0.321,"el":"N"},{"x":4.633,"y":0.033,"z":0.042,"el":"N"},{"x":1.852,"y":0.277,"z":0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.873,"y":-0.225,"z":-0.045,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.48,"y":-0.627,"z":-0.121,"el":"C"},{"x":2.44,"y":-0.968,"z":-0.139,"el":"C"},{"x":2.648,"y":1.4,"z":0.228,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.857,"y":-1.121,"z":0.357,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.264,"y":1.065,"z":-0.37,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.183,"y":-0.706,"z":0.421,"el":"C"},{"x":3.824,"y":-1.036,"z":-0.133,"el":"C"},{"x":4.023,"y":1.226,"z":0.218,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.471,"y":0.604,"z":0.074,"el":"C"},{"x":0.125,"y":1.341,"z":0.232,"el":"H"},{"x":1.921,"y":-1.9,"z":-0.289,"el":"H"},{"x":2.222,"y":2.387,"z":0.374,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.612,"y":-2.144,"z":0.629,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.573,"y":1.82,"z":-0.